# Response headers Cloudflare Pages adds to every route of this build.
# Copied to the site root verbatim by Astro, like everything else in public/.
#
# The one policy here is the Content-Security-Policy. It is hygiene, not an
# allowlist: `object-src 'none'`, `base-uri 'self'`, `frame-ancestors 'self'`
# and `form-action 'self'` close the classic injection routes, and
# `upgrade-insecure-requests` turns a stray http:// asset into an https://
# request instead of a blocked one (the mixed-content failure that most often
# breaks ad delivery). Script, frame, image and connection sources are any
# https origin on purpose.
#
# They used to be a list of named hosts, and that is exactly what the ad
# partner says not to do: programmatic advertising runs real-time auctions
# across dozens of exchanges, and the winning bidder serves its creative,
# pixels and redirects from a domain the last impression did not use. No
# allowlist stays complete, and every gap is an ad that silently fails to
# render. Mediavine's own guidance is a nonce-based `strict-dynamic` policy or
# `upgrade-insecure-requests`; a static site cannot mint a per-response nonce,
# so this is the latter, with the hygiene directives kept.
#
# 'unsafe-inline' is in script-src because the theme bootstrap in SEOHead.astro
# and the JSON-LD blocks in JsonLd.astro are inline; 'unsafe-eval' because the
# partner lists it among what its stack may need. connect-src stays open because
# the analytics and flag-delivery hosts are per-environment build settings this
# static file cannot know.
#
# The three headers under the policy are the rest of the baseline: nosniff stops
# a response being executed as a type it did not declare, Referrer-Policy keeps
# the path of the page a visitor is reading out of the request that fetches an
# ad (the origin still goes, which is what the partner needs), and HSTS keeps
# this site off plain HTTP for a year. The HSTS is deliberately narrow: no
# `includeSubDomains`, because sibling hosts (images.sleekdrops.com,
# go.sleekdrops.com) are served by other configs this file knows nothing about
# and a year is a long time to break one, and no `preload`, because that is a
# listing that cannot be withdrawn quickly.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https:; font-src 'self' data: https:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' data: blob: https:; frame-src https:; child-src https: blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' https:; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
